     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Section ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-1.1"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-1.1",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " defines a memento:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Memento: A Memento for an Original Resource is a resource that",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "encapsulates a prior state of the Original Resource.  A Memento",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "for an Original Resource as it existed at time T is a resource",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "that encapsulates the state the Original Resource had at time T.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "It seems that there may be some gray area here.  What exactly do we mean by \"prior state\".  For binaries the answer is clear enough.  For RDF not as clear. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
