      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Section <a href=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-1.1\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-1.1</a> defines a memento:<br/>\nMemento: A Memento for an Original Resource is a resource that<br/>\n      encapsulates a prior state of the Original Resource.  A Memento<br/>\n      for an Original Resource as it existed at time T is a resource<br/>\n      that encapsulates the state the Original Resource had at time T.<br/>\nIt seems that there may be some gray area here.  What exactly do we mean by \"prior state\".  For binaries the answer is clear enough.  For RDF not as clear. </p>",
